  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"1296\" data-end=\"1765\">\n<li data-start=\"1296\" data-end=\"1566\">\n<p data-start=\"1298\" data-end=\"1324\"><strong data-start=\"1298\" data-end=\"1323\">Decreased Factor VIII</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1566\">\n<li data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1375\">\n<p data-start=\"1329\" data-end=\"1375\"><strong data-start=\"1329\" data-end=\"1345\">Hemophilia A</strong> (X-linked recessive disorder)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1378\" data-end=\"1435\">\n<p data-start=\"1380\" data-end=\"1435\"><strong data-start=\"1380\" data-end=\"1406\">von Willebrand disease</strong> (vWF stabilizes Factor VIII)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1438\" data-end=\"1476\">\n<p data-start=\"1440\" data-end=\"1476\">Liver disease (synthesis impairment)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1479\" data-end=\"1525\">\n<p data-start=\"1481\" data-end=\"1525\">Disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1528\" data-end=\"1566\">\n<p data-start=\"1530\" data-end=\"1566\">Autoimmune inhibitors to Factor VIII</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1568\" data-end=\"1765\">\n<p data-start=\"1570\" data-end=\"1596\"><strong data-start=\"1570\" data-end=\"1595\">Increased Factor VIII</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"1765\">\n<li data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"1623\">\n<p data-start=\"1601\" data-end=\"1623\">Acute stress or trauma</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1626\" data-end=\"1653\">\n<p data-start=\"1628\" data-end=\"1653\">Inflammation or infection</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1656\" data-end=\"1667\">\n<p data-start=\"1658\" data-end=\"1667\">Pregnancy</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1710\">\n<p data-start=\"1672\" data-end=\"1710\">Use of estrogen-containing medications</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1713\" data-end=\"1765\">\n<p data-start=\"1715\" data-end=\"1765\">Increased risk of <strong data-start=\"1733\" data-end=\"1765\">venous thromboembolism (VTE)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-start=\"1772\" data-end=\"1781\">Notes</h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1783\" data-end=\"2080\">\n<li data-start=\"1783\" data-end=\"1893\">\n<p data-start=\"1785\" data-end=\"1893\">Always interpret Factor VIII levels in context with other <strong data-start=\"1843\" data-end=\"1864\">coagulation tests</strong> (like aPTT, PT, vWF levels).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1894\" data-end=\"1967\">\n<p data-start=\"1896\" data-end=\"1967\">In Hemophilia A, <strong data-start=\"1913\" data-end=\"1944\">aPTT is typically prolonged</strong>, but <strong data-start=\"1950\" data-end=\"1966\">PT is normal</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1968\" data-end=\"2080\">\n<p data-start=\"1970\" data-end=\"2080\">If Factor VIII levels are low but no family history or clinical bleeding, <strong data-start=\"2044\" data-end=\"2065\">inhibitor testing</strong> may be needed.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
